@startuml
title S-CORE Lifecycle Collector | Access Pattern Sequence
skinparam backgroundColor #F5F5F5
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #4F5D75
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #2D3142
skinparam sequenceParticipantFontColor #2D3142
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #7A8399
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam noteBorderColor #BFC0C0

' S-CORE source-side participants (blue/teal)
participant "Launch Manager" as LM #A8D8EA

' VEL Evidence Ingestion participants (green/amber)
participant "VEL Lifecycle\nCollector" as Collector #C5E1A5
participant "LifecycleFieldBindings\n(IStateFieldBindingProvider)" as Bindings #C5E1A5
participant "ConfigDrivenStateMapper\n(shared)" as Mapper #C5E1A5
participant "Schema Validator" as Validator #C5E1A5
participant "Normalization\nProcessor" as Normalizer #C5E1A5
participant "Vehicle Evidence\nPublisher" as Publisher #C5E1A5

== Initialization & Event Subscription ==
Collector -> Bindings : subscribe(on_update)
note right of Bindings
  * Collector passes on_update callback to Bindings;
    Bindings independently registers with LM.
    Collector is not a party to the LM registration.
end note
Bindings -> LM : register ext_monitor_notify callback\n(via IExtMonitorNotify event service)
LM --> Bindings : registration confirmed

== Asynchronous Event Push (on process/monitor state change) ==
LM -> Bindings : ext_monitor_notify callback\n(ProcessMonitorNotify payload)
Bindings -> Bindings : build new immutable snapshot\nand atomically swap it in
note right of Bindings
  * ProcessMonitorNotify payload delivers:
  * process identity (process_name, process_group_name)
  * process state (ProcessState), pid
  * graph state (GraphState)
  * exit_code, process_execution_error
  * supervision_status, failed_supervision_type
  * failed_supervision_cycles, deadline_error
  * heartbeat_error, logic_error, deadline_violation
  * alive_indication_count, process_group_id
  * recovery_state
  * Supervision fields originate from Health Monitor (PHM);
    LM is the callback emitter to LifecycleFieldBindings.
  * state, pid, graph_state are delivered via this push --
    VEL does NOT call ProcessInfoNode::getState()/getPid()
    or Graph::getState() directly; those are Launch Manager
    daemon-internal classes not reachable cross-process.
  * LifecycleFieldBindings builds one immutable snapshot
    struct from the full payload and atomically swaps it in,
    so subsequent read_field() queries within one collection
    cycle all observe the same notification generation.
  * Implements shared IStateFieldBindingProvider
end note

== Collection Cycle ==
Collector -> Mapper : map_to_raw_record(bindings)

group Pull Field Read (synchronous API call)
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("run_target")
  Bindings -> LM : get_active_run_target()\n(via ILmControl service)
  LM --> Bindings : run_target string
  note right of Bindings
    * run_target is the ONLY pull field from LM, via the
      synchronous ILmControl::get_active_run_target() API
      (Startup/Off/Fallback).
    * All supervision/state/pid fields are push-only via
      ext_monitor_notify (never polled via
      get_active_run_target()).
  end note
  Bindings --> Mapper : run_target value
end

group Cached Push Field Reads (from local cache)
  note over Mapper, Bindings
    * Bindings takes a single atomic snapshot of all cached
      push fields (an immutable struct swapped in on each
      ext_monitor_notify) at the START of this group -- not
      re-read individually per field.
    * read_field(field_name) is called once per field
      (IStateFieldBindingProvider signature:
      read_field(field_name: string)), but every call within
      this group resolves against that ONE snapshot.
    * Guarantees all push-origin fields in a single raw
      record originate from the same notification generation
      (no torn/mixed reads even if a new ext_monitor_notify
      arrives mid-cycle).
  end note
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("state")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.process_state\n(normalized to schema string)
  note right of Bindings
    * LifecycleFieldBindings normalizes C++ enum to schema
      string: kIdle->"idle", kStarting->"starting",
      kRunning->"running", kTerminating->"terminating",
      kTerminated->"terminated", kFailed->"failed"
  end note
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("pid")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.pid
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("graph_state")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.graph_state
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("exit_code")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.exit_code
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("supervision_status")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.supervision_status
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("failed_supervision_type")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.failed_supervision_type
  Mapper -> Bindings : read_field("process_execution_error")
  Bindings --> Mapper : snapshot.process_execution_error
  note right of Bindings
    * Remaining push fields (deadline_error, heartbeat_error,
      logic_error, deadline_violation, failed_supervision_cycles,
      alive_indication_count, process_group_id, recovery_state)
      follow the same one-field-per-read_field() call pattern,
      all resolved against the same snapshot taken above;
      omitted above for diagram brevity only -- never batched
      into a single multi-argument call.
  end note
end

Mapper -> Mapper : iterate score-lifecycle-state\nRawEvidenceSchema fields,\nbuild raw record generically
Mapper --> Collector : raw state record\n(score-lifecycle-state schema)
note right of Mapper
  * ConfigDrivenStateMapper is SHARED across every
    S-CORE module collector, not Lifecycle-specific
  * Driven entirely by the score-lifecycle-state
    RawEvidenceSchema config -- zero Lifecycle-specific
    logic in the mapper itself
end note

Collector -> Collector : produce collection_metadata\n(timestamp, duration, record_count=1 pre-populated)
note right of Collector
  * record_count is pre-populated as 1 for this cycle.
  * Final accepted/rejected count is reflected in health_status
    updated at the end of the cycle (after validation outcome).
end note
Collector -> Validator : raw state record + collection_metadata
alt schema-valid
  Validator --> Collector : schema-valid
  Collector -> Normalizer : validated raw state record
  Normalizer -> Publisher : normalized Vehicle Evidence
  Publisher -> Publisher : DDS publish\n(ScoreNormalizedEvidence, reliable)
  note right of Publisher
    * DDS reliable delivery: transport layer
      guarantees async delivery
    * Collector monitors VEL health via
      ScoreEvidenceLayerHealth topic
    * No synchronous ack from Publisher
  end note
else schema-invalid / reject
  Validator --> Collector : reject + AdapterDiagnostic
  Collector -> Collector : drop record,\nemit diagnostic
end

Collector -> Collector : update health_status\n(state, last_collection, collection_count,\nerror_count, last_error, uptime_seconds)
@enduml
